From: "R. Mark Sharp" <rmsharp@me.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:08:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(trim): an abort before the proof's checks exits 3, not 1,
 the FAIL code (issue #93; 1.8.1)

The generated proof's show() ended in sys.exit("verify: cannot read ..."), which prints the text
and exits 1 -- the FAIL code -- so a proof that could not read an artifact from git, and so had
compared nothing, read as a trim that lost something. Seen once in the adopter's 54-shard
--reverify sweep: a blob fetch from the partial clone's promisor remote failed and one shard read
FAIL; exit 0 on the re-run. Every abort before the checks (a git show that fails, a live or shard
file that cannot be read) now prints its reason to stderr and exits 3, the code the shell head
already uses and the code --reverify's legend gives "the proof did not finish". Frozen proofs keep
their bytes; --reverify renders today's template and reads 3 there. 203 tests (from 199), gate
199 -> 203; 6 mutants killed. On the adopter's 54 proofs: 46 exit 0, 8 exit 4, every shard as
under 1.8.0; with the promisor remote dead, --reverify reads 3 where 1.8.0 read 1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
